# Thesis voice (Walter, 11 Sep)

Full checklist: `.agents/context/writing/2026-09-11-review-loop-2-checklist.md`.

## Narrative

- **User-centric.** The study measures what advertising costs the user
  (trust, credibility, felt manipulation, attention). Not advertiser
  yield, not a serving rule. Abstract, Implications, Conclusion say so.
- **On Walter's side.** Critical, never destructive. A Holm-surviving
  result (posterior \(\alpha\) early−late; explicit-early onset tilt;
  trust × posterior \(\alpha\) \(\rho=.80\)) is stated as a finding
  first, then one caveat. Never "not greater visual processing",
  "the pipeline is not dead", "the dull readings win".
- **Answer the RQs.** Discussion carries `tab:rq-answers`; every RQ is
  answered positively or negatively. Unanswerable RQs are removed from
  the introduction, not left open.
- **Limitations ≠ Future work.** Ch 8 limitations = what the design
  could not see. Ch 9 future work = what to build next.

## Prose

- Paragraph titles are short noun phrases: `Temporal effects on memory
  and trust.` Never slogans, never Twitter.
- No WIP prose in the PDF. A gap is `% [AI: …]`, one line, critical only.
- No unexplained jargon: OR, GEE, lean, inventory, labelling. Define in
  one clause or drop.
- Positive Results paragraph models: the `tab:traj-aligned-counts`
  paragraph and the trust × posterior \(\alpha\) paragraph in 7.6.1.
- Short paragraphs. Never one blob per section.
- Direction always in words ("explicit is noticed more than implicit");
  magnitude optional.

## Names

- `contexts` (bare utterance vs deployed window fed to
  \(f_{\mathrm{genre}}\)), not `labellings`.
- `outcomes`, not `composites`. `banner` for the explicit unit, not `card`.
- \(k=37\) only in Ch 4 preprocessing and Methods. "\(u_5\) does not
  exist" once, in Results 7.5.
- Holm \(p\) = Holm-adjusted paired \(t\). Wilcoxon \(p\) is raw. No BH.

## Figures and tables

- Every figure is a vector PDF from matplotlib (`format="pdf"`, no
  `rasterized`). PNG only for UI screenshots.
- Every forest plot marks Holm \(p<.05\) with the same orange asterisk.
- Captions ≤ 2 lines. Tables: bold Holm-significant rows, family
  divider rules, "Key estimate" not "Headline".

## Comments in tex

- Keep every Walter line. Never delete one.
- `% WALTER:` is still open. `% WALTER+:` is addressed (same words, plus
  sign on the tag). Flip the tag when the ask is applied; do not invent
  a new comment.
- Add `% [AI: …]` only when the *how* needs one line. The `+` is the
  status. Grep open with `% WALTER:` and skip `% WALTER+:`.
- No agent instructions, lock pointers, or `[TODO]` drafts in the tex;
  those live under `.agents/context/`.
- Keep Gold-provenance comments (`% NUMBERS: analysis/walter/…`).
